  "narrative": {
    "intro": "At and T Enterprises has $917M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 218 awards this period, with an average award size of $4.2M, and obligations are down 11.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $167M in FY21 to a peak of $1B in FY25 before settling at $917M in FY26. Department-level demand is concentrated: the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $335M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $176M, and the Department of Justice obligated $154M in FY2026 to date. Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the dominant market for At and T Enterprises, with $901M obligated in that NAICS, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $10.7M. The firm’s federal revenue mix shows heavy reliance on telecommunications work and a small amount of services and equipment contracts across other NAICS. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations trended recently?",
        "body": "At and T Enterprises obligations grew from $167M in FY21 to $1B in FY25, then declined to $917M in FY26. Obligations are down 11.6% year over year. The company’s FY26 total of $917M is a partial fiscal year figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and what markets dominate?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer at $335M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $176M and the Department of Justice at $154M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest market at $901M, with Other Computer Related Services at $10.7M and All Other Telecommunications at $2M also represented."
      }
    ]
